fix(r2): use {bucket}/{key} — the colon form made wrangler reject the bucket

`npm run content:import -- --covers` died on its very first upload:

    The bucket name "lingoglasse-media:covers" is invalid.

r2Put/r2Get spelled the object path `{bucket}:{key}`, but wrangler 4.x wants
`{bucket}/{key}` — with a colon it split there and treated the whole string as
a bucket name. The message pointed at the bucket, so the real cause (an
argument shape) was invisible. This also silently broke the read side, so
sync-content could never pull covers back out of R2.

Result of the fix, verified against the real bucket:
- 5 covers uploaded and now in story_images as is_cover=1 (byte sizes match
  the repo files exactly; the object downloads back at 353340 bytes)
- sync-content reports "5 covers synced" instead of skipping them, and the
  export rewrites those 5 stories' frontmatter to the R2 URL
- public/images/covers/** is generated and deployed, so the reader resolves
  the new path

tests/scripts-d1.test.ts locks the argument shape down so a future wrangler
change fails a test instead of a production import. It also drops the
.commitmsg.tmp scratch file that git add -A swept into the previous commit.
